# launch-claude-season.rish — print the recipe for an unattended season run.
#
# The Rish preferred entry for running Claude Code across seasons inside ai-jail
# with every permission prompt skipped, so the recursion continues without a hand
# on each "Do you want to proceed?". This script PRINTS the recipe; it does not
# launch claude itself, because the jail launch belongs in your outer terminal
# (the same way `remember` keeps install lines on the operator desk). Copy the
# printed command, run it there.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/launch-claude-season.rish
#
# Discipline it keeps: safe by default (prints, never flips a bypass config for
# you); civic (custody note — the one irreversible rung stays manual); Lindy
# (the durable memory is the repo — REMEMBER, the logs, the plans — not a
# session id that resets with the jail).

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md not found)"

# invariant: the standing entry the recipe wraps must exist.
let elder = run ["test" "-f" "tools/agent-jail.sh"]
assert elder.ok else "tools/agent-jail.sh (the jail elder) is missing"

say "Claude Code — unattended season run inside ai-jail"
say "================================================="
say ""
say "One hard requirement: run as a NON-ROOT user. Claude refuses"
say "--dangerously-skip-permissions as root, and ai-jail is the sandbox this"
say "flag is meant for — so it is safe here, with nothing sensitive at risk."
say ""
say "1) Make the bypass standing (once) — gitignored, never reaches the seed:"
say "   in .claude/settings.local.json set  permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions"
say "   (the exact JSON renders in:  ./tools/agent-jail.sh --help)"
say ""
say "2) Launch — resume a specific session (placeholder RESUME_SESSION_ID):"
say "   ./tools/agent-jail.sh --resume=RESUME_SESSION_ID --dangerously-skip-permissions claude"
say ""
say "3) Or continue the most recent session in this repo:"
say "   ./tools/agent-jail.sh --continue --dangerously-skip-permissions claude"
say ""
say "0) Smoke test first — confirm -p runs in the jail (returns pong in seconds):"
say "   ./tools/agent-jail.sh --dangerously-skip-permissions claude -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say "   -p mode is HEADLESS — there is no interactive interface, and without"
say "   --verbose it prints nothing until the lap finishes (minutes). Silence"
say "   after the jail banner is the lap working, not a hang. --verbose streams it."
say ""
say "4) Most durable — one lap, a fresh session driven by the repo's own memory"
say "   (survives the jail resetting host HOME, where session ids live). One"
say "   line, copy whole (no line-continuation joins — copy the full line):"
say ""
say "   ./tools/agent-jail.sh --dangerously-skip-permissions claude --verbose -p 'Read work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md, then take the next agent-doable lap, Lindy-first crux-first, following the compass; witness on metal; send each round to origin and xykj61; STOP and surface, never cross, the custody gates in REMEMBER. baton prin recur'"
say ""
say "5) Continuous recursion — wrap the lap in an OUTER-shell loop that stops"
say "   itself when only custody gates remain. It lives in the outer terminal on"
say "   purpose: the jail launch belongs outside the jail, and an unbounded loop"
say "   is kept out of the tree's own TAME-bounded code (this .rish only prints)."
say "   One line, copy whole:"
say ""
say "   until ./tools/agent-jail.sh --dangerously-skip-permissions claude --verbose -p 'Read work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each round to origin and xykj61; STOP at the custody gates in REMEMBER; if only those gates remain print exactly GATES-ONLY and stop. baton prin recur' | tee /dev/stderr | grep -q GATES-ONLY; do sleep 20; done"
say ""
say "Custody note: the gates in REMEMBER stay MANUAL even in autonomous mode —"
say "the seed force-push, provisioning and paying, funds and keys, and the"
say "maintainer's own Kumara instance. Everything else may run unattended;"
say "reds-first, witness-before-narrative, and Lindy-first are seated rules, so"
say "the recursion stays disciplined on its own."
say ""
say "GREEN: season-run recipe printed — copy a command above into your outer/jail terminal."
